---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Terms & Conditions — VatSnap"
  description="VatSnap terms: free guidance tool, not tax advice. Acceptable use, embed attribution, and liability limits."
  canonicalPath="/terms/"
>
  <h1>Terms &amp; Conditions</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Free to use, with common-sense limits. Last updated: September 2026.
  </p>
  <div class="card">
    <h2>1. What VatSnap is</h2>
    <p>
      VatSnap is a free, unofficial VAT rate calculator for small online
      sellers. Rates are bundled at build time from the open-source
      <code>eu-vat-rates-data</code> package (source: European Commission
      TEDB). We aim for accuracy but make no guarantee that any rate is
      current or applicable to your situation.
    </p>
    <h2>2. Not tax advice</h2>
    <p>
      Everything on this site is general guidance, not professional tax, legal,
      or accounting advice. VAT treatment depends on place of supply, customer
      status, product category, thresholds, and exemptions that a calculator
      cannot know. Always confirm with a qualified adviser or the official EU
      source before invoicing or filing. You use the results at your own risk.
    </p>
    <h2>3. Acceptable use</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Use the calculator and country pages for lawful purposes.</li>
      <li>Do not attempt to disrupt the site, scrape it abusively, or misrepresent it as an official EU source.</li>
      <li>Do not remove or obscure the "guidance only" disclaimers when quoting results.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>4. Embedding</h2>
    <p>
      You may embed the free mini calculator via the snippet on our
      <a href="/widget/">Embed page</a> on any lawful website. Please keep the
      "Powered by VatSnap" link intact so the free service can sustain itself.
      We may change or retire the embed endpoint at any time.
    </p>
    <h2>5. Intellectual property</h2>
    <p>
      Site design and explanatory text are ours. VAT rates themselves are facts
      sourced from the open dataset described above — see the linked package
      and EU TEDB for their licensing.
    </p>
    <h2>6. No warranty &amp; liability limit</h2>
    <p>
      The site is provided "as is", without warranties of any kind. To the
      maximum extent permitted by law, we are not liable for any loss arising
      from use of, or reliance on, the calculator or its rates — including
      incorrect filings, missed deadlines, or business decisions.
    </p>
    <h2>7. Changes</h2>
    <p>
      We may update these terms at any time by posting a new version here.
      Continued use of the site after changes means you accept them.
    </p>
    <h2>8. Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about these terms? Reach us via the
      <a href="/contact/">Contact page</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
